MID_LGV_3_M04_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kai_m01_001: A while back, I found bandits being attacked by the\nrisen dead. I helped them out, but...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kai_m01_002: it upset a few people. They shouted, "Why are you\nhelping them? They're bandits!" I got so mad.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kai_m01_003: So, I yelled back, "People can be anything if they're\nstill alive!" I got laughed at, but I made my point.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Kai_m01: <BLN>I got so mad.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bel_m01_001: There was a man at the colosseum who compared\nme to a monoceros.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bel_m01_002: "Fragile, but strong," he called me.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bel_m01_003: At the time, I didn't think much of it...but it's\nlingered in my memory.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bel_m01_004: Poor Gabriel. If I saw him now, I wonder how\nI'd respond.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Bel_m01: <BLN>A man I knew.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dit_m01_001: ...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dit_m01_002: What is the nature of pleasure? I was pondering this.\nNo matter what befalls the world, I do not change.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Dit_m01: <BLN>...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tal_m01_001: Thanks to the ongoing destruction of Dagda, the\ncoffee industry has all but collapsed.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tal_m01_002: I'd planned to sell the company's remaining stock, but\nagain, Balor is getting in the way of a good thing.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tal_m01_003: There's a rumor now that Dagdan coffee curses you\nto die young! But I'd be long dead if that were true.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Tal_m01: <BLN>How am I gonna sell this stuff?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Orh_m01_001: When I chat with people in the city, many say\nthey feel uneasy at night.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Orh_m01_002: They can't sleep because they're scared of when\nthe risen dead might attack again.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Orh_m01_003: When I see someone suffering like that, I try to\nlook after that person as long as I need to.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Orh_m01_004: They can often fall asleep once they feel calm\nand comforted.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Orh_m01: <BLN>Many feel uneasy...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Seo_m01_001: Your title of Promised One inspires soldiers and\ncitizens alike.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Seo_m01_002: The citizens are drawn by the legend of the Herald,\nwhile the soldiers admire your skilled leadership.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Seo_m01_003: But now that you have won their trust as a leader,\nyou must take great pains not to lose it.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Seo_m01: <BLN>"Promised One" is an inspiring title.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Led_m01_001: The Rose Pageant, where the Rose of Caelus is\nchosen, hasn't been held since Solel's death.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Led_m01_002: I asked Kalla—it sounds like she doesn't intend to\nhold any more, even after the war.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Led_m01_003: Which disappointed me. But of course, the sadness in\nher eyes was greater.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Led_m01_004: It's not as if I have any say in the matter. All I can do\nis play whatever song she requests.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Led_m01: <BLN>The Rose Pageant...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Anh_m01_001: I get a bit emotional when thinking about the ancient\npeople who once lived here.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Anh_m01_002: As queen of Solomon, I'll see to it that records of\nthem are passed on to the future.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Anh_m01_003: I can't afford to die here. I have to survive, so I can\nbring us victory.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Anh_m01: <BLN>I must pass this on to the future.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tia_m01_001: I'm keeping a record of battles with the risen dead so\nfuture generations will have precise information.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tia_m01_002: I read so much history that helped my planning. It's\nmy turn to pass knowledge forward.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Tia_m01: <BLN>I'm keeping a record...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pet_m01_001: Urgh... I still throw up after a battle.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pet_m01_002: And, given that I've been fighting for so many years,\nI feel pathetic.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pet_m01_003: I've really seen a lot of things since that first fight.\nPeople killing, being killed...
MID_LGA_3_M04_Pet_m01: <BLN>I'm still not over it...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hur_m01_001: I didn't become a priest because of my faith.\nI did it because I needed a job.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hur_m01_002: Now that the temples are such a mess, I'm much\nmore aware of my duties as a priest.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hur_m01_003: Even with everything in a shambles, I want to be\nable to hold my head up high in front of Aurora.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Hur_m01: <BLN>I became a priest because...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Max_m01_001: Sometimes my fellow soldiers ask me out for a drink.\nI don't like drunks, so I always tended to decline.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Max_m01_002: Now I find that it's nice to have a tipple once in\na while—go out and share a laugh over a glass.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Max_m01_003: Though...I must have a pretty high tolerance, because\nit always ends with me being the others' caretaker.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Max_m01: <BLN>It's kind of nice.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gol_m01_001: I've been helping! Not just in fights, but with repairs\nand stuff too.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gol_m01_002: I'm carrying heaps of materials, liftin' up workers\nto reach roofs and stuff...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gol_m01_003: and when rubble comes falling down, I smash it\ninto pieces. Gotta keep the others safe!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Gol_m01: <BLN>Not just fighting!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gat_m01_001: Finally! Euhhh... There was a squire who was so\ninsistent about helping me.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gat_m01_002: It's not as if I need someone fussing over me\nin battle. I'm not some helpless old man.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gat_m01_003: Still, I suppose I appreciate his concern...so I'll have\nto do my best to keep the risen dead's hands off him.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Gat_m01: <BLN>Finally!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dan_m01_001: Lately, it's fallen upon poets to craft epitaphs for\nthe graves of the fallen.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dan_m01_002: So that the dead, soldiers and otherwise, are never\nforgotten, we write verse to celebrate their deeds.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dan_m01_003: I only hope these words of prayer ward off any\ndisturbance in their rest.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Dan_m01: <BLN>My newest works.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fab_m01_001: These insects are truly fragile. They perish so easily,\nsuccumbing to even a glancing wound.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fab_m01_002: Not that I mind, per se. It is, in fact, convenient in\nsome ways.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fab_m01_003: Yet each of their deaths increases the strength of our\nfoe, Balor.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fab_m01_004: As it makes what is already a troublesome situation\nbleaker, I wish they could simply stand aside.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Fab_m01: <BLN>Do not involve yourselves...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Esm_m01_001: Ever heard of Cetus, the Sea Tyrant? The\nmassively powerful sea monster?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Esm_m01_002: I actually got Grasitha, my spear, from fighting her\nalongside Sweetie.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Esm_m01_003: Wielding it kinda makes me feel like Cetus is right\nthere with me. It's a big confidence booster!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Esm_m01_004: If you've never met it, count yourself lucky. Every\nsailor knows and fears that thing.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Esm_m01: <BLN>Have you heard of Cetus?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Urs_m01_001: Hm? Why are you looking at me like that?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Urs_m01_002: If you're worried about me, don't be. I'll be fine,\nI promise.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Urs_m01_003: Please, go. Everyone is waiting for you.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Urs_m01_004: If I end up needing you, trust me, I wouldn't call\non anyone else.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Urs_m01: <BLN>I'm alright.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sim_m01_001: You know... Sometimes I feel like the world is better\nthe way it is now.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sim_m01_002: Every day, we have to beat back death and fight for\nour next breath. To me, that's a beautiful way to live.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sim_m01_003: But... If I feel happiness, that must mean normal\npeople are just suffering through this...
MID_LGA_3_M04_Sim_m01: <BLN>Why do I feel this way...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lou_m01_001: Jurah, Mars, Smyrnos, Credna, Kalla, Fortuna...\nBe with us now.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lou_m01_002: The temples may have lost some of their power, but I\ncan still pray!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Lou_m01: <BLN>Guide us...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fia_m01_001: In the past, I would panic when so many injured\npeople were brought in...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fia_m01_002: Now, I can tell who to treat first just by examining\ntheir wounds.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fia_m01_003: If I can teach what I've learned to the other healers,\nwe'll be able to save even more lives.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Fia_m01: <BLN>I used to panic, but no more.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Die_m01_001: The risen dead aren't mindlessly attacking the living.\nThey have souls and intelligence.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Die_m01_002: So, you never know what they'll do, or where\nthey'll attack from. Stay vigilant. Send out scouts.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Die_m01: <BLN>The risen dead...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lor_m01_001: After working for Credna's temple for so long,\npeople say I've gained a lot of skills.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lor_m01_002: Even Ozin smiled and said he's got nothing much\nleft to teach me.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lor_m01_003: Maybe, if I wanted to, I could become a vulkan\nlike Ninae... Heh, I mean, not really.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Lor_m01: <BLN>People say I've got skills now!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Set_m01_001: One of my favorite dishes ever is one made from\nherring and fruit. Its sweetness is quite interesting.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Set_m01_002: This dish furthermore warms your heart when you\neat it. Have you ever eaten something like that?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Set_m01_003: Come to think of it, we've been seeing more\nallies from Fódlan of late.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Set_m01_004: Some act quite...suspiciously. Well, I suppose\nwe need all sorts of allies in this crisis.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Set_m01: <BLN>A curious thought...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nin_m01_001: The notion of a "god of death" applies much more\nto Balor than it ever did Yu Phas...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nin_m01_002: Yu Phas guided souls into the cycle of life and\ndeath. That was the spirit of her teachings.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nin_m01_003: She's being forgotten as an evil god these days,\nbut I don't want her to be forgotten entirely...
MID_LGA_3_M04_Nin_m01: <BLN>A god of death...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bon_m01_001: This army is formed from people of various creeds,\ncombat styles, and reasons for fighting.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bon_m01_002: It may be inappropriate of me to admit this, but as\na warrior, I find that exciting.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Bon_m01_003: I hope that I can add my intelligence and prowess\nto the heady brew.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Bon_m01: <BLN>I hope I shall have a place in this.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tob_m01_001: I've gotta find some time to recount all the military\nachievements I racked up over the past few years.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tob_m01_002: There's usually a celebration-of-service ceremony\nafter a war. Wouldn't look good if I forgot my own.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tob_m01_003: At my age, remembering all my achievements is an\nachievement in itself!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Tob_m01: <BLN>Gotta recount my achievements.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lil_m01_001: Honestly, my Yu Phas worship used to be mostly\nlip service.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lil_m01_002: But we live in a world where life is cheap and the\ndead come back, which got me thinking.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lil_m01_003: "Hey, maybe Yu Phas was guiding souls to keep the\nworld from getting this way."
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lil_m01_004: So now when I pray to her, I mean it.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Lil_m01: <BLN>Honestly, I barely believed in her.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lys_m01_001: This constant fighting has left no time for lighter\nfare. I hate to see the children growing bored.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Lys_m01_002: Would it be appropriate to hand out the throwing\nsticks I make as a hobby?
MID_LGA_3_M04_Lys_m01: <BLN>Would it be appropriate...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Buc_m01_001: The civilians here. I'm helping them in battle, and\ntraining...and with their laundry! So much laundry.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Buc_m01_002: They say it's because I'm so thorough. I know, I did\nbecome skilled in the task through Lady Leda.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Buc_m01_003: I just wish it wasn't so hard to say no when they\nkeep showering me with gratitude...
MID_LGA_3_M04_Buc_m01: <BLN>Gods!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sci_m01_001: When bards in the future sing of this war, and of us,\nwhat will they say?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sci_m01_002: I expect their masterpieces will outshine all other\nepics written thus far...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sci_m01_003: and that I'll steal even more women's hearts from the\npopularity. Now, that's enticing.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Sci_m01: <BLN>When the bards sing their songs...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Moo_m01_001: While you were away, I started sparring with\nthe soldiers.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Moo_m01_002: But they went easy on me. The nerve! You know\nhow annoyed that made me?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Moo_m01_003: Then I fought and fought until they took me\nseriously. And accepted me as the real deal.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Moo_m01_004: Then they started calling me "big sis," which...\nNot sure how to feel about that.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Moo_m01: <BLN>So frustrating!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mic_m01_001: I never even considered there'd be a situation the\ntemples couldn't deal with!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mic_m01_002: We all thought that as long as the gods were here,\nnothing could happen.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mic_m01_003: And then the god of the underworld pops up and\ntries to destroy everything... Who could imagine it?
MID_LGA_3_M04_Mic_m01: <BLN>Just goes to show!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Oly_m01_001: I'm often asked how, in such dark times as these, I\ncan bear to continue performing.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Oly_m01_002: But people are grieving. It is precisely because of the\nworld's terrible state that I continue.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Oly_m01_003: I feel impelled to draw upon the power of dance,\nthat I might ease the people's despair!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Oly_m01: <BLN>I will dispel it!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Naz_m01_001: It's kinda funny. I managed to keep our secret\nuntil the world fell apart...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Naz_m01_002: Yet nobody questions us since we're all part of the\nsame army under your banner, Promised One.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Naz_m01_003: Before, I mighta got annoyed about how they all\nchanged their attitude so quick.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Naz_m01_004: But I guess it's fine, since we're your allies.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Naz_m01: <BLN>It's kinda funny.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sar_m01_001: Zenon had enough faith in my mother to entrust\nAnatolia and Nezha to her care.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sar_m01_002: But apparently she wasn't told anything about you,\nPromised One.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sar_m01_003: I've always wondered just what happened between\nyou and Zenon.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Sar_m01: <BLN>I've always wondered...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dai_m01_001: Sometimes people ask me to fix stuff like farming\ntools because I'm good at tinkering.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dai_m01_002: That stuff's easy, compared to something as\nadvanced as a Salamander.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Dai_m01_003: Funny thing is, we didn't have farming tools back in\nthe village, so I thought they were weapons at first!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Dai_m01: <BLN>Fixing that stuff's easy.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hal_m01_001: My family had a farm, but it was on borrowed land.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hal_m01_002: I heard they escaped a risen-dead attack, and now\nthey're living in the city.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hal_m01_003: I wonder if the fields maybe got destroyed? Not that\nfields are much good unless you're alive.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Hal_m01: <BLN>My family...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Guj_m01_001: Soldiers, priests, and the like...seem to respect me\nmore recently.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Guj_m01_002: They finally appreciate that I'm Unkillable Guzran.\nBecause, you know...I'm unkillable.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Guj_m01_003: They buy me drinks now! I'm saving so much\nmoney. I have Balor to thank for all this!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Guj_m01: <BLN>I really owe Balor!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Yan_m01_001: To be revived when you die... What a tragedy.\nLife is such suffering.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Yan_m01_002: Thinking upon this, I decided to mourn the dead\nthat I defeated by creating a grave for them.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Yan_m01_003: Then I was immediately attacked by them again!\nSo I took the headstone and clobbered them all.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Yan_m01: <BLN>I mourned the risen dead, but...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Iio_m01_001: I tried drinking mead a while ago. It didn't make me\nfeel very good.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Iio_m01_002: I got light-headed and my legs grew wobbly. I was\ntold it'd be fun...like stumbling through a dream.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Iio_m01_003: But that was wrong—and I didn't like it. I'd rather\nget through this life without stumbling.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Iio_m01: <BLN>I tried mead, but...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pep_m01_001: The entire citizenry of Dagsion was boiled down in\nDagda's cauldron... Death, for all of them...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pep_m01_002: But! We have learned that the children from lower\nDagsion who helped us have...returned to the city!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pep_m01_003: They all came back safely. We shared with them how\nglorious and magnificent this news was to us!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Pep_m01_004: They laughed at our royal verbiage! Do they still not\nknow us to be a king? But we are glad they are safe.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Pep_m01: <BLN>How joyous in the end!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Noc_m01_001: The risen dead are trouble for everyone, but they\nare the perfect training partners. 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Noc_m01_002: You have to be so careful when you're training with\nthe living not to ruin them—or kill them!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Noc_m01_003: But you can fight your hardest against the dead.\nYou can hit them with ALL you've got!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Noc_m01: <BLN>The risen dead are trouble, but...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sop_m01_001: I got called the Grumbling Tummy for the first time\nin a long time. Ha! That little kid's all grown up...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sop_m01_002: But I actually got called...Dagsion's Most\nGrumbling Tummy. That seems a little too much.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Sop_m01_003: Yes, my stomach's always speaking up, but is it\nworth calling out as "most" anything? Really!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Sop_m01: <BLN>It's a little much...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cat_m01_001: The quality of goods has dropped drastically due to\nthis war. There's nothing suitable for you and me!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cat_m01_002: Have no fear, Promised One. You'll be able to get\nthe very best soon enough, if you keep me near.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cat_m01_003: I know that if you gather enough sterling people\ntogether, top-notch goods appear soon enough!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Cat_m01: <BLN>Have no fear...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ned_m01_001: My friends among the Saramis soldiers look\ndifferent than the last time I saw them.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ned_m01_002: They've survived this nightmare. They've lost\ncomrades. They're growing tough as warriors.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ned_m01_003: It's a welcome sight for a mercenary like me. But\nit's also hard to see younger people suffer.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Ned_m01: <BLN>Inspiring, and yet...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Zac_m01_001: One of the nearby villages had a few houses\nleft standing...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Zac_m01_002: A bandit's gotta do what a bandit's gotta do! Raze\nthe place! But yeah, I gotta hold back...maybe.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Zac_m01: <BLN>I gotta hold back...maybe.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Maj_m01_001: The dead can rise all they want, but they're no\nmatch for the great Majide on a rampage!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Maj_m01_002: So hey, you keep your small-time allies back,\nOK? They gotta stay alive to cheer me on!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Maj_m01: <BLN>Leave it to the great Majide!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ven_m01_001: I'm working myself to the bone. Why are there no\nportraits glorifying General Benditz everywhere?!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ven_m01_002: Oh, at least one rosy youth ought to have captured\nmy likeness out of sheer admiration by now.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ven_m01_003: Of course, I have a somewhat senior visage, but I\nam handsome in profile! Is it the eye patch?
MID_LGA_3_M04_Ven_m01: <BLN>Most troubling!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ini_m01_001: I heard that Ugo's Bow used hair from those\nterrible remains for its string.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ini_m01_002: It's hard to believe that they made a weapon as\npowerful as that using only some hair.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ini_m01_003: I...can't imagine how powerful a revived Balor\nmust be.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Ini_m01: <BLN>Just from hair...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jas_m01_001: Even at times like this, it's important to laugh\nonce in a while.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jas_m01_002: When you're down in the dumps, your thinking\nisn't at its best.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jas_m01_003: So by laughing just like this—ha ha ha haaa!—you\ncan feel your whole self come back to you.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Jas_m01: <BLN>It's important to laugh!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ale_m01_001: Bucephalus was tiny when I first met him.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ale_m01_002: He wouldn't eat much feed either, so I used to\nworry about the little guy.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ale_m01_003: But after we tried out a few different kinds of feed,\nI found one he liked. Then he ate his fill.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ale_m01_004: Though I did get a real scolding from a doctor, given\nI was feeding him just that one thing all the time!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Ale_m01: <BLN>When I met Bucephalus...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cen_m01_001: As "Corundum Centurio," it is my duty to train the\ntemple's soldiers each and every day.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cen_m01_002: Naturally, I haven't skipped a single day of my own\ntraining either. I'm quite proud of that.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cen_m01_003: If my old friend Castor were here, he'd tease me.\nHe'd say, "You never do change!"
MID_LGA_3_M04_Cen_m01: <BLN>It is my duty...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kir_m01_001: How can the rest of the world get messed up...and\nthe Vandahl Trading Company still doesn't fail?!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kir_m01_002: I can't just wait around for that to happen. Even\nBalor isn't going to take a tumble without a push.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kir_m01_003: So when this war ends, I'll go after that company\nmyself! I'll tear it down with my own hands!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Kir_m01: <BLN>Why don't they fail?!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nuz_m01_001: Saramis has been a haven for us. We're gradually\ngrowing closer to its people.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nuz_m01_002: They are not, unfortunately, the only people with\nwhom the Har Hali have burned bridges.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nuz_m01_003: I want to believe I can show my people a new way—\na path of coexistence between children of Damascar.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Nuz_m01: <BLN>My people are improving.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_001: The eternal life of a god is an eternal prison.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_002: Though they seem vast to you, even the heavens\nare a cage formed of powerful causality.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_003: To live eternally is to remain bound to this world.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_004: The longer one lives, the more lives you see end.\n'Tis a never-ending procession of farewells.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_005: In time, all things—all people—will travel to a far-off\nland where she and I cannot follow.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_006: We are imprisoned by our existence.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Fot_m01_007: Freedom that is not won for oneself is a fleeting\ndream that remains ever elusive.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Fot_m01: <BLN>Eternal life...eternal prison.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_001: I feel a kinship with Queen Theodora and the other\nchildren of Damascar.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_002: In them, I see the son who was torn from me so\nlong ago.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_003: <NCA>"I can see why."
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_004: Even if he survived and found refuge in Cybele,\nmy son was an ordinary human.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_005: He would have reached the end of his natural life\nmany years ago.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_006: But then I think of how his bloodline—those who\ninherited his nature—might still be with us.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Kou_m01_007: I find it an encouraging thought...even if it is merely\nwishful thinking.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Kou_m01: <BLN>I feel a kinship with Damascar.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tro_m01_001: Quite a few people have returned to Dagsion by now.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tro_m01_002: You can see in their faces that they're starting to\nrediscover their hope for tomorrow.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tro_m01_003: It's a welcome change from the last few years\nof despair.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Tro_m01: <BLN>People are returning.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Asw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Asw_m01_001: I'm rather surprised. I never thought I'd ever see\nDagsion so restored!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Asw_m01_002: Exuberance everywhere, after all the despair we'd\nbeen engulfed in.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Asw_m01_003: But I suppose that's the sign that the people are\nuniting around their savior.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Asw_m01: <BLN>It was a surprise.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tah_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tah_m01_001: My husband was a guard for King Hasdrubal. \nPassed away a few years ago.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tah_m01_002: Maybe if he was alive, His Majesty wouldn't have\nbeen assassinated.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tah_m01_003: And the chancellor wouldn't have been able to drive\nBertrand out of the country.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Tah_m01_004: Then again, who can say how a different past would\nhave affected our current circumstances.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Tah_m01: <BLN>My dear husband.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nat_m01_001: He sets loyalties aside to follow his heart—to do\nwhat's right.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nat_m01_002: Bertrand's no less upright than when I knew him as\na general.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Nat_m01_003: In truth, it may be I envied him.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Nat_m01: <BLN>Bertrand.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hri_m01_001: So many beautiful women! It can't be so bad to let\nloose around them.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hri_m01_002: What's with the look? I need a break!
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hri_m01_003: But you, too, have a divine beauty, Promised One.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Hri_m01_004: What say you and I meet up and discuss the future\nover a couple glasses of ghosh? Once in a while?
MID_LGA_3_M04_Hri_m01: <BLN>Hmm? Hmmm?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ann_m01_001: After I left the temples, I spent some time traveling\nthe land of Dagda.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ann_m01_002: But after a while, I felt the urge to give the merchant\nlife a serious try.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ann_m01_003: It's fun! Being a go-between from suppliers to clients\njust feels right to me somehow.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Ann_m01_004: And it doesn't hurt that I've made a bundle in\nthe process!
MID_LGA_3_M04_Ann_m01: <BLN>Being a merchant is fun.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mys_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mys_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mys_m01_003: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mys_m01_004: 
MID_LGA_3_M04_Mys_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cle_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cle_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cle_m01_003: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cle_m01_004: 
MID_LGA_3_M04_Cle_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gra_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gra_m01_001: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gra_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Gra_m01_003: 
MID_LGA_3_M04_Gra_m01: 
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jun_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jun_m01_001: Credna and Kalla are the children I bore with\nDagda the Great.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Jun_m01_002: They both have their quirks, but I think they grew\ninto people I can be proud of.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Jun_m01: <BLN>Credna and Kalla...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01_001: When I heard the Divine Emperor had suddenly gone\nto sleep, and that my brother was taking his place...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01_002: I had a lot to say about it. And I went to Solel\nin protest.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01_003: It was plain that Jurah, Dagda's second in\nthe hierarchy, should have replaced him.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01_004: But she refused to do so. So I was out in the cold.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Mar_m01_005: All I could think to do was suggest a match between\nHanno and Breza to calm the tension.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Mar_m01: <BLN>Know what I said?
MID_LGV_3_M04_Smi_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Smi_m01_001: I must say, I'm quite fond of cats. It's because of\ntheir unpredictable nature.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Smi_m01_002: I never get tired watching them. They're so hard\nto predict.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Smi_m01: <BLN>I'm quite fond of cats.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cla_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cla_m01_001: How strange... The way you've taken command\nof things in Dagsion, it's almost as if...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cla_m01_002: Well, it's as if you've done this for a long time.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Cla_m01_003: You carry yourself with such confidence. That's so\nunlike me. I'm apprehensive to a fault at times.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Cla_m01: <BLN>How strange...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01_001: Following the example of others in my family, I went\ninto the city to play vihuela for the refugees.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01_002: I hope I was able to help them forget their worries\nand find some comfort.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01_003: And for my part, I realized how long it had been\nsince I'd felt such enjoyment while performing.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01_004: There I was, feeling the simple joy of making art,\nsomething I'd long forgotten.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Car_m01_005: I suppose the true essence of art is far removed from\nrank or prestige.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Car_m01: <BLN>I was playing my vihuela.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_001: I understand the circumstances, but you mustn't\npush yourself too hard.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_002: You serve as a beacon of hope. For all of us.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_003: I know you take care of yourself, but please keep\ndoing so.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_004: When I look at you, Father... And at Mother...
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_005: I feel so uneasy.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_006: I know all that has happened is a matter between\nhusband and wife.
MID_LGV_3_M04_Aur_m01_007: And that, as your daughter, there is so much I will\nnever be able to understand.
MID_LGA_3_M04_Aur_m01: <BLN>Take care of yourself.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B01_m01_001: Ten years ago, I was a gladiator, and I had Gabriel\nlooking out for me.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B01_m01_002: I was strong, but my heart wasn't in it. He gave me\nsome farewell money and sent me back home.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B01_m01_003: Everyone will tell you how miserly he could be.\nBut deep down, he was generous at heart.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B01_m01: <BLN>He had a heart of gold...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B02_m01_001: Hunting bears gets you meat and fur, but hunting the\nrisen dead gets you nothing. I do it anyway, though.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B02_m01_002: They only exist to kill us. You can't take that kind\nof thing lying down.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B02_m01: <BLN>I hate the risen dead.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B03_m01_001: I'd rather be doing distance running than spear drills.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B03_m01_002: Escaping the risen dead would be way more useful\nthan making a futile stand against them.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B03_m01: <BLN>Hmmm.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B04_m01_001: Until a little while ago, it was tough to get enough\nfeed for horses and war elephants.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B04_m01_002: When the famine was at its worst, we had no choice\nbut to slaughter the weaker ones to feed ourselves.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B04_m01_003: It was necessary, but it hurt that the most I could do\nfor them was to give them a painless death.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B04_m01: <BLN>Until a little while ago...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B05_m01_001: I'm so hungry...but I have to bear it. If I don't eat,\nthere'll be more food for the soldiers.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B05_m01_002: If I can't fight, taking care of the ones putting their\nlives on the line for us is the least I can do.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B05_m01: <BLN>I'm so hungry...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B06_m01_001: When the statue of Lord Solel was built, I said it was\ndisrespectful to reproduce the face of a god.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B06_m01_002: Few agreed with me, and now I'm glad they didn't.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B06_m01_003: Now that statue will always stand as a reminder of\nLord Solel, our revered Sunbearer.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B06_m01: <BLN>Lord Solel's statue...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B07_m01_001: I've wondered something for a while now...how did\nwe come to see the gods as gods?
MID_LGV_3_M04_B07_m01_002: I suppose when you're face to face with divine\nbeauty like Kalla's, the natural instinct is to kneel.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B07_m01: <BLN>I've been wondering...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B08_m01_001: Gods! Oh gods! Save my grandchild, I beg you!
MID_LGV_3_M04_B08_m01_002: The other day, when risen dead attacked the village...\nI'm certain I saw my granddaughter among them.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B08_m01_003: She was such a sweet child who wouldn't hurt a fly!\nFor her to end up as one of those abominations is...
MID_LGA_3_M04_B08_m01: <BLN>Gods! Oh, gods!
MID_LGV_3_M04_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B09_m01_001: The fields are all ruined thanks to the demon god,\nbut we're all pitching in to try to cultivate them.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B09_m01_002: Even if I die, the seeds I sow today might end up\nfeeding my children.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B09_m01: <BLN>We're cultivating the fields.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B10_m01_001: I bought a shield from a merchant who assured me it\nwas guaranteed to protect me from any monster.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B10_m01_002: But it was just a board with a painted-on design.\nFell apart after taking a couple of hits.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B10_m01: <BLN>I've been swindled!
MID_LGV_3_M04_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B11_m01_001: Dad won't let me go outside of Dagsion. He says\nit's dangerous.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B11_m01_002: But it's so boring here! Promised One, tell me a\ngood story!
MID_LGA_3_M04_B11_m01: <BLN>It's so boring here!
MID_LGV_3_M04_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B12_m01_001: The grown-ups are all fed up. They're mad the war\nhas been going on for longer than five years.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B12_m01_002: I'm eight, so I don't really remember before the war.\nWhat's peace like?
MID_LGA_3_M04_B12_m01: <BLN>What's peace?
MID_LGV_3_M04_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B13_m01_001: My big sis is a great ornius rider! She's tough,\nshe's carefree, and she's terrific.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B13_m01_002: Last I saw her, she was heading out to save an\nisolated village. But that was months ago...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B13_m01_003: She probably just got lost on her way back. I really\ndon't think she'd up and die so easily.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B13_m01: <BLN>She must be somewhere...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B14_m01_001: Before the war, I had some modest fame as a\nshoemaker in Urka.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B14_m01_002: But the war made materials scarce, so I had to close\nup shop. I'd like to reopen someday if I can.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B14_m01: <BLN>Once the war's over...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B15_m01_001: There are quite a lot of refugees here who all got on\na boat and came to Dagsion by sea.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B15_m01_002: But I worry that our enemies will get the same idea.\nWe have to keep our eyes open.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B15_m01: <BLN>We have to stay alert!
MID_LGV_3_M04_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B16_m01_001: I'm a coward who got fed up with this never-ending\nwar and deserted my squadron.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B16_m01_002: But I haven't forgotten how to fight. Nothing my\nsuperiors drilled into me has gone away.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B16_m01_003: Now I protect the refugees from the risen dead. They\nseem grateful, so maybe deserting wasn't so bad.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B16_m01: <BLN>I'm not a total coward...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B17_m01_001: I'm no regular soldier with formal training. Just some\nguy who took a bit of equipment off a corpse.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B17_m01_002: But standing around in this getup makes the kids\nfeel safer.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B17_m01_003: I'm in way too deep now to back out...but I'll leave\nthe real foe-smiting to you, Promised One.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B17_m01: <BLN>The truth is...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B18_m01_001: No matter how dismal this world gets, as long as\nanyone's left alive, then demand will exist.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B18_m01_002: And merchants will be the ones to supply them!\nWe'll go anywhere to close a deal!
MID_LGA_3_M04_B18_m01: <BLN>Even in this dismal world...
MID_LGV_3_M04_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B19_m01_001: A favorite pastime of nobles was to watch bouts in\nthe arena, mocking those who fought for spectacle.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B19_m01_002: But the same ones we laughed at were the ones who\nsaved us when the risen dead attacked.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B19_m01_003: Knowing full well how we used to mock them,\nno doubt. I'm ashamed.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B19_m01: <BLN>I'm ashamed of myself.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_3_M04_B20_m01_001: I visit here every so often.
MID_LGV_3_M04_B20_m01_002: I still feel like maybe...maybe I'll see her again after\nwe were separated four years ago.
MID_LGA_3_M04_B20_m01: <BLN>I can't let go...